So, here it is.  My second ascension.

This game was really pretty easy and straightforward.  (Before I
ascended, I always hated people referring to Nethack as "easy"!)

An altar in the very first room granted Mjollnir after a few
sacrifices.  A magic lamp in an early shop soon yielded sweet, sweet
blessed fixed +0 grey dragon scale mail (I usually go for +5, just
'cause it's so fun when it works.  :)

It wasn't too long before I wandered across some speed boots.  Sokoban
yielded a bag of holding (I HATE getting reflection in Sokoban. 
Typically by this point in the game, I'm stuffed to capacity and
really need a bag).

In Minetown, I found a famous bones x2 level.  My earlier wizard died
once, left a bones, and then the next one died again, leaving bones
again.  This was great, because on that level was another magic lamp
(or two?!) and I think gauntlets of power.

I also found a pair of magic markers pretty early on, and soon enough
I had enchanted my base AC way down, and my survivability skyrocketed.

The quest was super easy, due to the fact that someone somehow
insta-killed Lord Sartur.  I think he was hit by an errant wand of
death or something.  I didn't really see it happen.

I found the vault and cleaned that out without much issue, and dropped
by AC some more by donating.

At Medusa's level, I had some close calls with a pair of giant eels. 
There were two next to me, and one wrapped itself around my leg.  I
was pretty sure that one was already there, and the other just moved
up, so I teleported (I learned to keep a wand of teleportation handy
after my last drowning!) the stationary guy away and was able to
escape.  That was a really close call.

The castle gave me a wand at 0:1.  I think I wished for some scrolls
of charging and at some point I know I wished for a shield of
reflection and a helm of telepathy to round out my armor.  I think
another magic marker, as well.

Gehennom was straightforward.  I got most of the way down, and then
decided to do some nurse dancing, so I headed back up to Sokoban,
clearing a path between the stairs on each level on the way up (I
forget about the Orb of Fate level teleport ability!).  But clearing
paths like this is handy.  Nurse dancing gave me a piddly 3 nurses,
who helped me out a little bit.  Not as much as I would have liked. 
I've never done any alchemy, and don't really know how it works, but
most of my potions went to make holy water anyway.

Headed back down again, found the vibrating square by accident, and
headed back to kill the wizard.  Didn't mess around with him, but
blasted him with a wand of death, grabbed the Amulet, and headed back
down.  Had the amulet soon enough, and started what I thought would be
the race to the top.  It was a hell of a climb, though, as I kept
getting sucked back down (this happens more for lawfuls, right?). 
Eventually got out, and made it to the planes.  Only my second time
here.

Earth was easy.  I basically killed everything on the level, then
wandered around and found the portal.

Fire was pretty easy as well.  Again, I basically extincted everything
and searched for the portal.

Air, which everyone says is the hardest, wasn't that bad.  I ran to
the right side of the screen, and after killing almost everything, did
some vertical runs until I found the portal.

The ol' Astral plane.  I decided to head away from Death (since I had
some charges in my wands o' death), so I started going up the middle. 
Found Famine.  Used my wand of death on him, and found the altar to be
Neutral.  Headed left.  Found Pestilance.  He got me sick, and my
blessed unicorn failed 4 times!  I eventually was able to heal and
blast him, but it was pretty scary (I did have blessed potions of full
healing and an amulet of life saving on, but still).  That altar was
Chaotic.

So, back to Death.  I beat him down hand to hand pretty easily (he
only drained me once for just a few), and all of a sudden, there I
was.  It always surprises me that it just takes one final step, and
then you're there, at the altar, ready to ascend.

Nothing fancy, in spite of wishes to burn.  Offered and ascended for
my second ever ascenscion.  Good stuff.

This was the first game I played using the hjklyubn keys, and I really
enjoyed it.  No more arrow keys for me!

Here's the ol' dump.  Thanks for reading.


